{"id":"9bc3a38b-348d-4e55-a4ee-c4791dc42c60","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The main method is always invoked by the JVM with a non-null args array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.785928Z"}
{"id":"a39a85da-b47b-47a2-aef8-2357be8773f5","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array lengths in Java are always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.785928Z"}
{"id":"ff9c9bdb-2274-49ed-9956-06da39fffa2a","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The method parameter 'args' is never set within the method, so it remains as passed. The program point is at method exit, so this must remain true unless the method changes it.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.787001Z"}
{"id":"afc4cdd6-425d-4a08-a459-384cf8c0fdd1","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"In Java, array length is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.787001Z"}
{"id":"eb96f57e-aaa7-4ecf-879e-b432a45c70b0","expr":"a != null","rationale":"The method uses a methods and instanceof checks, so a should be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.787960Z"}
{"id":"a2763bb9-f182-4d42-a514-82481314c9db","expr":"b != null","rationale":"The method calls b.doubleValue() and b.intValue(); b must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.787960Z"}
{"id":"9b4f77ec-5603-4e1b-bb58-17ac6611b132","expr":"a.getClass().equals(b.getClass())","rationale":"The operation uses methods like intValue or doubleValue on both; inconsistent types may not be handled.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.787960Z"}
{"id":"33af3243-6b30-48a7-a137-79c96f5e1ac0","expr":"b == null || b.doubleValue() != 0.0 || result == null","rationale":"If b is not null and its double value is zero, the result is null to indicate division by zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.788369Z"}
{"id":"d9d6c50f-a48a-415d-b349-b33d408b0bed","expr":"result == null || a != null","rationale":"A returned non-null result implies that a must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.788369Z"}
{"id":"5eaa16b7-5743-43f4-9a9c-c29aea1a518e","expr":"result == null || b != null","rationale":"A returned non-null result implies that b must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.788369Z"}
{"id":"ad46a8c9-6d86-463f-ab20-459b5d725f31","expr":"result == null || b.doubleValue() != 0.0","rationale":"A non-null result implies division by zero did not happen, so b.doubleValue() != 0.0.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:48.788369Z"}
